         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Introduction\n\nThe next number of the decimal system is the number one (1), and it also carries a special characteristic in its multiplication table, which we are going to learn in this class.\n\nRemember from our previous classes: multiplying is a fast way of adding the same number many times. And remember the table of zero: no matter what we multiplied by zero, the answer was always zero.\n\nNow we will see that multiplying by one is also special: the result always keeps the number we started with. Because of this, every answer of the multiplication table of one is equal on both sides of the equality.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
